Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ZeusLock agent: managed configuration (Windows registry policy scope).
; Fill in YOUR_SERVER_URL and YOUR_LICENSE_KEY below, then either:
;   * import on a reference machine:  reg import ZeusLock-Policy.reg
;   * or replicate these values via a GPO Registry preference (recommended for
;     fleets: see docs/01-windows-gpo.md, Method B.2).
;
; A license key here makes the PC "managed": users cannot quit the agent.
; Optional settings (docs/configuration-reference.md) go in the same key: strings are
; REG_SZ ("..."), on/off settings REG_DWORD (dword:00000001 = on, dword:00000000 = off).
;
; The license key is a secret. Importing this file leaves the key with the default
; permissions of HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies (readable by every account on the machine,
; services included). Restrict it to SYSTEM + Administrators (full) and INTERACTIVE
; (read): run Install-ZeusLockAgent.ps1 (Method A does it for you), or push the
; permissions with the GPO setting "Security Settings > Registry" - see
; docs/01-windows-gpo.md, B.2. Delete your filled-in copy of this file afterwards.
;
; Start at sign-in needs nothing here: the MSI adds it (HKLM\...\Run "ZeusLock Agent").

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\ZeusLock]
"ServerUrl"="YOUR_SERVER_URL"
"LicenseKey"="YOUR_LICENSE_KEY"
